      "content": "It's completely valid to feel that way when you've lost a significant part of who you were. That feeling of being a shell, like your foundation is gone, is a profound kind of grief. Sometimes, the pressure to \"rebuild\" feels overwhelming when the original structure is gone. Perhaps instead of rebuilding, just focusing on the smallest, most immediate needs—like getting through the next hour—might feel less daunting.",
